docs {
  # ro-builder API

  Hand-curated [Bruno](https://www.usebruno.com/) collection mirroring
  `api/openapi.yaml`. The OpenAPI spec is the contract; this collection
  is one consumer of it. When the spec changes, update the matching
  request body or response handling here.

  ## Requests
    1. `score`; calc-direct sample (Swordsman vs Poring)
    2. `generate`; enqueues an async LLM-driven build generation (TK
       PvM defaults from `scripts/generate.sh`); returns 202 + an id
       that the post-response script stashes as `generationId` and
       `savedBuildId`
    3. `generation-status`; polls `/generations/{id}`; re-run until
       `status` is `completed` or `failed`
    4. `get-saved-build`; pulls the enriched saved trajectory and
       renders a rocalc-style endgame view (mirrors `generate.sh`)
    5. `list-builds`; recent saved trajectories

  ## Environments
    - `local`; `http://localhost:8080` (matches `task run:api` and
      `task docker:up` defaults)

  ## Typical flow
    1. Run `generate` → enqueues; the id flows into both `generationId`
       and `savedBuildId` automatically.
    2. Run `generation-status` repeatedly (every ~30s) until it reports
       `status=completed` (success) or `status=failed` (gave up).
    3. Run `get-saved-build` to render the endgame trajectory with
       catalog-resolved item / card / skill names.

    Bruno's "Run Folder" runs them once each in sequence; useful for a
    quick smoke, though you'll usually want to re-run step 2 a few
    times while the worker is busy.
}

auth {
  mode: none
}
